      "start_seconds": 0.84,
      "end_seconds": 4.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.84,
      "end_seconds": 9.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.49,
      "end_seconds": 16.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "So the thing is I've got pain in my right shoulder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.59,
      "end_seconds": 19.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.31,
      "end_seconds": 25.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Probably three weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.71,
      "end_seconds": 29.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.73,
      "end_seconds": 35.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "it's moderate, honestly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.39,
      "end_seconds": 38.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.19,
      "end_seconds": 42.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "it just comes and goes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.72,
      "end_seconds": 45.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "anything that improves it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.0,
      "end_seconds": 49.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Ice helps a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.92,
      "end_seconds": 67.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "have you had swelling by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.14,
      "end_seconds": 69.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "nope no swelling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.8,
      "end_seconds": 77.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Any fall or injury, numbness or neck pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.63,
      "end_seconds": 80.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.2,
      "end_seconds": 84.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.31,
      "end_seconds": 88.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.48,
      "end_seconds": 93.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Alright is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.63,
      "end_seconds": 95.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.55,
      "end_seconds": 98.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.65,
      "end_seconds": 102.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "No surgery no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.27,
      "end_seconds": 106.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.38,
      "end_seconds": 112.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Cat fur. I come out in... well, sneezing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.97,
      "end_seconds": 122.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine work habits that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.13,
      "end_seconds": 139.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.11,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.06,
      "end_seconds": 155.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.0,
      "end_seconds": 159.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Losartan 50 milligrams once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.02,
      "end_seconds": 177.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.08,
      "end_seconds": 181.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I've, I've got high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.4,
      "end_seconds": 190.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "right right. Right so high blood pressure is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.03,
      "end_seconds": 204.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Right I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.32,
      "end_seconds": 219.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "That's it, just a a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.95,
      "end_seconds": 239.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "okay: respiratory rate 14 blood pressure 125 over 79. And And pulse 76 oxygen saturation is 97 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.75,
      "end_seconds": 241.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Is that that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.72,
      "end_seconds": 247.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.97,
      "end_seconds": 252.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.99,
      "end_seconds": 256.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.28,
      "end_seconds": 284.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "There is pain when you lift the arm out to the side between about sixty and one hundred and twenty degrees and the grip strength is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.86,
      "end_seconds": 303.77,
      "duration_seconds": 13.91,
      "text": "okay, that's enough for me putting it all together, I'm honestly not certain yet it could be a rotator cuff tendon problem, or it might be neck-related arm pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.85,
      "end_seconds": 308.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.03,
      "end_seconds": 327.99,
      "duration_seconds": 17.96,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a a rotator cuff tendon problem do well once it's treated properly let's get a shoulder X-ray, for shoulder pain it's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.01,
      "end_seconds": 331.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.95,
      "end_seconds": 359.98,
      "duration_seconds": 28.03,
      "text": "Let's use naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day with food, for one week. You take it by mouth. That should help with shoulder pain. Keep the shoulder moving gently within comfort and avoid heavy overhead lifting. Do get help quickly if the arm becomes numb or you get fever. Book a review in four weeks. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.67,
      "end_seconds": 364.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "no that's all thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.74,
      "end_seconds": 371.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
